Z||000000||lennyb4||06-01-2000||09:08 AM||||Ok guys i know this has been discussed before but i cant remember what thread it was in. I know there isnt alot of difference between the 87 Coupe and the 87 Formula. What exactly is the difference? Im thinking rear wing and decals?<P>And what do you guys think about turning my coupe into a formula? Yes-No||||reg||5
Z||000001||ChadMan||06-01-2000||09:40 AM||||There was no Formula in 87 - Pontiac added the Formula to the lineup and dropped the SE in 88.<P>The Formula is mechanically a GT (same drivetrain, suspension, steering) but has Coupe bodywork and interior, plus a wing and 15" black lace wheels.||||reg||1
Z||000002||fiero56||06-01-2000||10:07 AM||||Don't forget the v-6. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>There are many of us Formula owners on the forum. A Formula, is basically an '88GT with coupe body panels. Interior is also a little different.||||reg||1
Z||000003||2M4 Dale||06-01-2000||10:35 AM||||Or a coupe is a Formula sans the v6 and the wing...lol<P>Do it Lenny !!!||||reg||1
Z||000004||fiero56||06-01-2000||11:02 AM||||Don't forget the stickers, or the rear sway bar. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Plus, we have rally guages, verticle redline tach, and all those other goodies too. heehee. Makes me want to outside and drive it right now.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/formulabarn.jpg"> ||||reg||1
